 "answer": "**Singapore’s air is currently poor because of haze.** The latest official NEA readings I found—reported at **6 p.m. on October 15**—were **24-hour PSI 121–186 (Unhealthy)** and **1-hour PM2.5 95–208 µg/m³** across regions. NEA’s forecast for **October 16** is **Unhealthy to Low Very Unhealthy**. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-15-october-2026))\n\nFor a more immediate but unofficial snapshot, IQAir showed **US AQI 252 (“Very Unhealthy”) at 9 p.m.**; that uses a different scale from Singapore’s PSI. ([iqair.com](https://www.iqair.com/sg/air-quality/singapore/singapore/singapore))\n\nIf you’re outside, check NEA’s latest **1-hour PM2.5** for your area before exercising; consider avoiding strenuous outdoor activity, especially if you’re sensitive to haze. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-15-october-2026))",
